\newcommand{\StudyInterpretation}{%
The paired tables isolate a finite-retraction/reset effect from the bias-gain effect. Noise/population-prior controls and the condition-specific scores are retained in the CSV, including numerical failures and missing convergence. The conditional excitation monitor and the full nuisance-eliminated window information use different assumptions; agreement is not presumed. Fixed-time normalized NEES ensemble bounds are [0.73, 1.31]. All covariance statements remain conditional on the declared CARMA, sensor-noise, calibration and bias priors. The one-Hz Ljung--Box diagnostics and all p-values are retained in the JSON; they are descriptive serial tests, not new independent trials. Supplying the exact field changes TFG horizontal-bias RMS from 51.95 to 46.51 mm/s$^2$; it does not remove the remaining error. Matching the packet-noise model gives 58.34 mm/s$^2$ and normalized serial NEES 11.32, so packet-noise mismatch alone does not explain the weak bias estimate. Across the recorded bias-held startup nodes the maximum TFG/TAN physical difference is 0.000000; startup is shared rather than a source of the geometric comparison.  At the unadjusted 5\% level, 50 of 126 axis/seed/method whiteness tests reject; these correlated multiple tests are not independent acceptance votes.%
}
\newcommand{\StudyRecommendation}{%
Do not promote the tangent-bias geometry or the conditional gain veto as a new production default from this evidence. Retain the experimental implementation and transfer only independently validated shared corrections. Geometry and a conservative gain policy have not jointly established the required accuracy, consistency, robustness and target qualification.%
}
\newcommand{\ValidationResults}{%
Validation receipts, untouched-main parity and pinned-replay outcomes are recorded in \texttt{validation.json}; they must be read alongside the statistical cohort.%
}
